  "definition": "Optical space communication transfers information through free space on a modulated optical carrier, usually a laser. A link can connect two spacecraft or a spacecraft with an airborne or ground terminal. Current Consultative Committee for Space Data Systems standards specify physical-layer parameters for non-coherent optical links, providing an interoperability baseline rather than a complete terminal design.[^1]",
